The Lean failure is reproducible and specific: this sandbox reports an inner PID from `getpid()` while `/proc` is mounted in the outer PID namespace; Lean 4.22 constructs `/proc/<getpid()>/exe`, so executable discovery fails. I’m applying a narrow build-only shim that makes `getpid()` return the numeric target of `/proc/self` for Lean/Lake processes. This changes no source, theorem, or proof term; I’ll record the shim source, hash, compilation, and all build commands.
